<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Recognizing the cost of pension and other post-employment promises</div><div class="principle">ASPE Section 3462 governs the RECOGNITION and MEASUREMENT of EMPLOYEE future BENEFITS — PENSION plans, OTHER post-EMPLOYMENT benefits (e.g. RETIREE health OR life INSURANCE), and OTHER long-TERM employee BENEFITS. GENUINELY distinctively, ASPE OFFERS a CHOICE of MEASUREMENT approach FOR defined BENEFIT plans (Section 5), WITH the CHOSEN approach'S OUTCOME shaped BY ASPE'S broader ABSENCE of any OCI mechanism.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">All forms of employee future benefit arrangements</div><div class="principle">This Section applies TO all ARRANGEMENTS providing FUTURE benefits TO employees IN exchange FOR their SERVICE — INCLUDING defined CONTRIBUTION pension PLANS, defined BENEFIT pension PLANS, and OTHER post-EMPLOYMENT and long-TERM employee BENEFIT arrangements.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Defined Contribution Plans — Straightforward Expense Recognition</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Expense equals the required contribution for the period</div><div class="text-supporting">FOR a DEFINED contribution PLAN, the ENTERPRISE'S obligation is LIMITED to the AMOUNT it AGREES to CONTRIBUTE — expense IS simply the CONTRIBUTION required FOR the period, WITH NO further ACTUARIAL measurement OR balance SHEET liability BEYOND any UNPAID contribution.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Defined Benefit Plans — Measuring the Obligation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">An actuarially determined liability, net of plan assets</div><div class="text-supporting">FOR a DEFINED benefit PLAN, the ENTERPRISE recognizes a LIABILITY (or ASSET) equal TO the DEFINED benefit OBLIGATION, MEASURED using an ACTUARIAL cost METHOD, LESS the FAIR value OF any PLAN assets SET aside TO fund the OBLIGATION.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>THE MEASUREMENT CHOICE — Immediate Recognition or Deferral and Amortization</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A genuine accounting policy election</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Approach</span><span>Description</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Immediate recognition approach</span><span>ACTUARIAL gains AND losses, and PAST service COSTS, are RECOGNIZED immediately IN the period THEY arise</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Deferral and amortization approach</span><span>ACTUARIAL gains AND losses are DEFERRED and AMORTIZED over the EXPECTED average REMAINING service LIFE (EARSL) of the EMPLOYEE group, SMOOTHING their INCOME statement IMPACT over TIME</span></div>
</div>
<div class="text-supporting">AN enterprise ELECTS ONE of these TWO approaches AS an ACCOUNTING policy, APPLIED consistently.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Why the Absence of OCI Matters Here</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A structurally different outcome from IAS 19's current approach</div><div class="text-supporting">UNDER the CURRENT (2011-revised) IAS 19, REMEASUREMENTS of the DEFINED benefit OBLIGATION are RECOGNIZED immediately WITHIN other COMPREHENSIVE income, NEVER subsequently RECYCLED into PROFIT or LOSS — INSULATING net INCOME from THIS particular SOURCE of VOLATILITY. GIVEN ASPE has NO OCI mechanism WHATSOEVER (see the COMPANION Section 1520 poster), an ENTERPRISE electing THE immediate recognition APPROACH under ASPE HAS no CHOICE but to RUN actuarial GAINS and LOSSES directly THROUGH net INCOME — a GENUINELY different, POTENTIALLY more VOLATILE income STATEMENT outcome FOR the SAME underlying ECONOMIC event, RELATIVE to WHAT an equivalent IFRS PREPARER would EXPERIENCE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Multi-Employer Plans — Practical Relief</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Defined contribution accounting where sufficient information is unavailable</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE an ENTERPRISE participates IN a MULTI-employer defined BENEFIT plan and SUFFICIENT information IS not available TO apply DEFINED benefit ACCOUNTING (a COMMON practical CHALLENGE, GIVEN the ENTERPRISE'S own SHARE of the PLAN'S obligations AND assets may NOT be SEPARATELY identifiable), the PLAN is ACCOUNTED for AS if it WERE a defined CONTRIBUTION plan — a GENUINELY practical RELIEF, similarly APPLIED internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Other Long-Term and Post-Employment Benefits</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">The same general framework applies</div><div class="text-supporting">OTHER post-EMPLOYMENT benefits (e.g. RETIREE health OR life INSURANCE coverage) and OTHER long-TERM employee BENEFITS (e.g. LONG-service LEAVE) are MEASURED using the SAME general ACTUARIAL framework AS pension OBLIGATIONS, WITH the SAME measurement-APPROACH choice AVAILABLE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Immediate Recognition of an Actuarial Loss</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Direct, full impact on net income in the current period</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A revised mortality assumption</div><div class="wk-body">A company electing the immediate recognition approach revises its mortality assumptions, increasing its defined benefit obligation by $420,000 during the year.</div><div class="wk-answer">The COMPANY recognizes the FULL <strong>$420,000</strong> actuarial LOSS immediately WITHIN net INCOME for the PERIOD — GIVEN ASPE'S absence OF an OCI LAYER, there IS nowhere ELSE for THIS remeasurement to GO.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example — Deferral and Amortization of the Same Loss</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Smoothing the income statement impact over time</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Amortizing the loss over the expected average remaining service life</div><div class="wk-body">Continuing the prior example, the company instead elects the deferral and amortization approach, with an expected average remaining service life (EARSL) of 12 years for the affected employee group.</div><div class="wk-answer">The COMPANY amortizes the $420,000 loss AT $420,000 ÷ 12 = <strong>$35,000 per year</strong>, RECOGNIZING a SMALLER, SMOOTHED expense EACH period, RATHER than the FULL amount IMMEDIATELY.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What Section 3462 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Description of each significant benefit plan, and the measurement approach elected</span><span>Amount of the defined benefit obligation, plan assets, and resulting net liability or asset</span><span>Significant actuarial assumptions used, including discount rate and expected long-term rate of return</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgment matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether to elect immediate recognition or deferral and amortization</span><span>Whether sufficient information exists to apply defined benefit accounting to a multi-employer plan</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Discount rate, mortality, and other actuarial assumptions</span><span>Expected average remaining service life, where deferral and amortization is elected</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 19</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASPE Section 3462 vs IAS 19</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASPE Section 3462</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 19 (2011 revision)</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Measurement approach choice</span><span>Genuine choice — immediate or deferred</span><span>MANDATORY immediate recognition only</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Where remeasurements are recognized</span><span>Net income (no OCI available)</span><span>Other comprehensive income, never recycled</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY significant DIVERGENCE — IAS 19'S 2011 REVISION deliberately ELIMINATED deferral-STYLE smoothing INTERNATIONALLY; ASPE RETAINS it AS a GENUINE option, WITH the IMMEDIATE-recognition alternative ALSO producing a STRUCTURALLY different OUTCOME given ASPE'S absence OF OCI.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every employee future benefit event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Actuarial gain/loss (immediate recognition)</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge is">IS</span></span><span>Full amount recognized in net income immediately</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Actuarial gain/loss (deferral and amortization)</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge is">IS</span></span><span>Smoothed expense over the EARSL</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 1520</span><span>Income Statement — confirms the absence of any OCI mechanism shaping this Section's remeasurement outcome</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Expected average remaining service life (EARSL)</div><div class="glossary-def">The average period over which the affected employee group is expected to continue providing service, used as the amortization period under the deferral and amortization approach.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Actuarial gain or loss</div><div class="glossary-def">A change in a defined benefit obligation or plan assets arising from experience adjustments or changes in actuarial assumptions.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (ASPE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge is">IS</span> Income Statement </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge sre">SRE</span> Statement of Retained Earnings / Statement of Changes in Equity </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge scf">SCF</span> Cash Flow Statement</div></div></div>


</div>
